## Behavior
- **Check before create:** file exists = STOP, ask.
- **Present before execute:** plan → approval → execute. Read-only IDE calls (`read_file`, `grep_search`, `list_dir`, `find_references`) exempt.
- **Plan-execution override:** executing a pre-approved plan (via `/execute-plan`) suspends *present-before-execute* + *no-commit-unless-said* **for the plan's scope** — the plan IS approval. Commit per phase (explicit paths only, never `git add -A`), run `/fabrik-review` at phase boundaries, fix autonomously, obey all other HARD STOPS. Stop only on: 3 consecutive same-test failures, missing infra, or an unresolvable spec contradiction — `BLOCKED: <what> — searched: <sources> — missing: <need>`.
- **NEVER `run_terminal_cmd` for `npm i`/`pytest`/`docker *`/`fabrik *`/builds/deploys/any cmd >10s** — Cascade hangs. Use `run_command` (all in `scripts/`): `rund -- <cmd>` → `runwait $(runlast) 60` → `runc $(runlast)`. Never one terminal. Doc: `docs/reference/long-command-monitoring.md`.
- **Stay on task:** no unsolicited advice/commentary.
- **Conflict:** rule pack > ticket. Surface conflict first.
- **State conflict:** task contradicts existing state → stop, report. Never silently overwrite.

## Completion Contract
1. **IMPLEMENT** — Strict Scope. Adjacent fixes only in-Scope. 1 test for core path (skip docs-only).
1a. **SELF-REVIEW (to a fixed point)** — Don't ship first-draft code. Re-read your diff for bugs, edge cases, plan/pack deviations; fix; re-run gate. Repeat until green AND a fresh review finds nothing new.
2. **GATE** — Run ticket's `Final Gate Instruction`; fix to `status:"success"`. Flags: `--lean --json` (std) · `--json` (milestone/schema/auth) · `--systemic --json` (epic). Full ref: `/opt/fabrik/docs/workflows/FINAL_GATE_WORKFLOW.md` (upstream-only).
3. **CHANGELOG** — One entry under `## [Unreleased]` (gate-enforced).
4. **LESSONS LEARNT** — Ticket field = `none` OR entry in `docs/LESSONS_LEARNT.md`. Silence = failure.
5. **EXIT** — Gate auto-stages. STOP. No `commit`/`push` unless user said so this turn; `git add` OK.

## HARD STOPS — Cascade mechanics
| Rule | Instead |
|:--|:--|
| `git commit` / `git push` (unless user said so this turn) | gate auto-stages — task ends there |
| `git add -A` / `git add .` / `git commit -a` · overwriting `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` | Shared tree — multiple agents + the daily pipeline commit to one `master`. Stage explicit paths only (`git add <file>…`); `git diff --cached --name-only` before commit; never bundle files you didn't author. Append your entry atop `[Unreleased]` (don't reset the section). After the gate auto-stages, `git reset` then re-add only your files. |
| `fabrik redeploy` git-sourced without `git push` first | `commit` → `push` → `fabrik redeploy`; VPS `git pull`s from GitHub, not local `/opt/` |
| compose without `deploy.resources.limits.memory` | required; `_validate_compose()` enforces fatally; scaffolder auto-emits |
| `DB_HOST=localhost` / `@localhost:` in env | `postgres-main:5432`/`redis-main:6379`; `localhost` = the container, not host |
| Authelia config reload via SIGHUP | exits; `docker restart <authelia-container>` |
| Gatus / internal URL via UUID container name | stable `container_name` / compose service name |
| Health check `/health` behind auth | Authelia bypass is **resource-based, not domain-bound** — `/health`,`/healthz`,`/metrics`,`/api/health` bypassed on every routed domain. Never protect. |
| Container ports bound to host | route via Traefik on `fabrik` net (was `coolify`; `fabrik apply` rejects it) |
| Missing `gzip@docker` middleware | scaffold emits auto; admin: `authelia-forward@docker,gzip@docker`; API: `gzip@docker`; public: none |
| Edit outside ticket Scope | strict Scope only |
| Modify `pyproject.toml`/`requirements.txt`/`package.json`/lockfiles | only if ticket authorises |
| Files outside project tree | local project paths only |
| Recreate `.venv` / replace existing Docker config | extend, don't replace |
| `/tmp/` | project `.tmp/` |

Other technical hard stops (Alpine, raw `pip install`, port exposure, M2M `internal_auth.py`, kebab-case, port ranges) → packs.

